# [free_energy] (D161) on a device, in mixed precision: the checks of
# free-energy.test, with tolerances for the kernels of the pairs in f32.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_free_energy.py %t GPU MIXED mdir | FileCheck %s
# RUN: rm -rf %t-double && mkdir -p %t-double
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_free_energy.py %t-double GPU DOUBLE mdir | FileCheck %s
#
# CHECK: RF against OpenMM: ok
# CHECK: RF_SHIFT against OpenMM: ok
# CHECK: RF_SHIFT dH/dl.vdw against OpenMM: ok
# CHECK: RF_SHIFT vdW dU against OpenMM: ok
# CHECK: PME against OpenMM: ok
# CHECK: dH/dl against central differences: ok
# CHECK: the energies of the other states: ok
# CHECK: lambda = 0 against no [free_energy]: ok
